cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MOONATLAS Science"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it together with the upstream scientific
  work it runs (see "references" and README § Citation). MOONATLAS claims no
  authorship of the NASA-IBM Lunar Foundation Model, the SomBench datasets or the
  reference catalogues.
type: software
authors:
  # Entity form: no personal contact information is published.
  - name: "The MOONATLAS contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/RRG1312/moonatlas-science"
url: "https://github.com/RRG1312/moonatlas-science"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible offline pipeline that runs the published NASA-IBM Lunar
  Foundation Model task checkpoints over the SomBench benchmark datasets and
  normalizes the raw model outputs into a validated, versioned lunar science
  dataset with full provenance. It covers crater detection on LROC WAC tiles,
  polar ice prospectivity regression and irregular mare patch segmentation on
  LROC NAC tiles, together with the geospatial, validation and reproducibility
  tooling needed to check the results independently.
keywords:
  - lunar science
  - remote sensing
  - foundation models
  - reproducibility
  - geospatial
  - crater detection
  - ice prospectivity
  - irregular mare patches
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.3.0"
# No DOI is claimed for this software. If it is ever archived (for example on
# Zenodo), add the DOI here and in README § Citation; never invent one.

# Metadata below is copied from the upstream model and dataset cards at the
# revisions pinned in src/moonatlas_science/config.py. Where the upstream cards
# give no venue or DOI, none is listed.
